# `todo/t1077` REGRESSION CELL — payload: `String`, storage class: `.rodata`
# LITERAL, consume shape: PRINT-DIRECT.
#
# ⭐ THE STORAGE CLASS OF A `String` PAYLOAD IS ITS OWN AXIS, and this cell is
# the WORST one in the whole class. `t1077` was filed on a HEAP-FORCED string
# (`box_nested_double_deref_reads_garbage.gg`, `mk(a, b)` so the value cannot
# be an immortal `.rodata` view), where C SIGSEGVs — loud. Write the obvious
# literal version instead and C exits 0 having printed NOTHING:
#
#   PRE-fix, C:    build rc 0, run rc 0, prints an EMPTY line   ← SILENT WRONG
#   PRE-fix, LLVM: build rc 0, run rc 0, prints `187651001414384`
#                  (a raw pointer as an integer)                ← SILENT WRONG
#
# Both lanes exit 0. No crash-watching gate can see this cell, which is exactly
# why `t1077`'s severity text had to be corrected: the class contains a
# silent-wrong face on BOTH backends, and silent-wrong-output outranks the
# SIGSEGV the item was named for.
#
# EXPECTED OUTPUT: hi
# EXPECTED EXIT: 0 on BOTH backends.
#
# ⛔ `known_gaps/` with a LIVE test: self-host cannot compile nested `Box`
# (`todo/t1311`) AND this leaks at scope exit (`todo/t1309`).

void main():
    Box[Box[String]] w = Box.new(Box.new("hi"))
    print((*(*w)))
